      "title": "Burnham vows crackdown on ‘rip-off’ business practices to ease cost of living",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2026/aug/09/burnham-vows-crackdown-on-rip-off-business-practices-to-ease-cost-of-living",
      "description": "<p>First of PM’s ‘everyday fixes’ to be banning fake discounts and making it easier to cancel unwanted subscriptions</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2026/aug/09/andy-burnham-british-people-ripped-off-cost-of-living\">Andy Burnham: I’ll end the rip-offs that people hate</a></p></li></ul><p>Andy Burnham has promised a series of measures to tackle the cost of living, including a ban on fake discounts and making it easier for people to escape unwanted subscriptions.</p><p>The crackdown on “rip-off” business practices is expected to benefit consumers to the tune of £400m a year and will be the first in a range of “everyday fixes” to be implemented in the coming months.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/business/2026/aug/09/burnham-vows-crackdown-on-rip-off-business-practices-to-ease-cost-of-living\">Continue reading...</a>",
